<onlyinclude>A '''digital ecosystem''' is a collection of interacting digital technologies, services, organizations and users whose activities depend on one another. An ecosystem may include platforms, applications, devices, shared standards and participants that maintain or use them.

== Explanation ==
A mobile application ecosystem includes device makers, developers, users, service providers and rules for distributing applications. Changing a platform interface can affect many otherwise separate systems. Some researchers also use the term for decentralized evolutionary software architectures.

